WEBVTT

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:49.382
I've got a favor to ask.

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:55.972
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:00:55.972 --> 00:00:59.517
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:00:59.517 --> 00:01:06.941
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:12.697
<i>Chizu o ushinatte samayotteiru machi</i>

00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:16.159
<i>Owariyuku sekai demo</i>

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:22.874
<i>Karada no oku de hashiru</i>
<i>no o yamenai inochi o kikasete</i>

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:26.169
<i>Tayasanai hikari o tozasanai hitomi ni</i>

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:29.547
<i>Kawaitemo yakitsuketa</i>

00:01:29.547 --> 00:01:36.137
<i>Kizutsuku koto mo naku</i>
<i>te ni suru mono nante nanimo shinjinai</i>

00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:42.060
<i>Dareka ni mukatta hitosuji no omoi wa</i>

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:49.943
<i>Yoake no you ni hagane no yami o kirisaku</i>

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:54.280
<i>Itsuka brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.951
<i>Dakara tsuyoku kaeru</i>

00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:03.915
<i>Kasaneta chikara mo inori mo</i>

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:07.585
<i>Kousa suru mirai, kakaeta negai</i>

00:02:07.585 --> 00:02:11.006
<i>Dare no te ni mo watasenai</i>

00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:12.549
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:17.512
<i>Kokoro o tsuraneru</i>

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:24.019
"The Fallen Ones Appear"

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.815
There's something I want to talk about...

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:33.028
It's Siena.
Would you let me take care of her?

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:34.779
Wait, Sharnid.

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:38.825
It's not as if we've
accepted the president's proposal yet.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:42.203
Then is there some other way?

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:49.210
Please listen. It's a foolish story...

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.297
We'd been friends since our first year.

00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:56.301
We got along crazy well
almost immediately after we met.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:09.564
And it was the former leader
of the 10th Platoon who looked out for us.

00:03:15.487 --> 00:03:20.700
She was a great person.
We thought young, foolish things

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.703
like "Let's give our all for her."

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:56.736
When we lost the last intermunicipal battle,

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.738
she was so sad.

00:03:58.947 --> 00:04:02.951
She hated that she'd
graduate not being able to help Zuellni.

00:04:16.881 --> 00:04:20.593
When we saw her like that,
we made a promise:

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:24.222
that we would protect Zuellni ourselves.

00:04:26.182 --> 00:04:27.600
But...

00:04:27.809 --> 00:04:33.314
Rifts had already started to form between us.

00:04:33.314 --> 00:04:36.651
It would've been fine
if things had just fallen apart...

00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:39.029
But instead, I only half-broke us.

00:04:39.029 --> 00:04:42.991
Then <i>he </i>clumsily tried
to make the pieces fit together.

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:47.454
That's why, this time...

00:04:50.915 --> 00:04:52.751
Understood.

00:05:19.069 --> 00:05:21.321
<i>Did you see that, Sharnid?</i>

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:25.450
<i>I can still do it, even without you!</i>

00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:34.751
Keep pushing, Siena!
We're going to cream them!

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:39.089
Traps 1 and 2 have been destroyed.

00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:40.715
That was fast.

00:05:40.715 --> 00:05:44.094
<i>It didn't even slow them down.</i>
<i>You're good, Dinn.</i>

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.347
Lay-ton...

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.599
What?!

00:05:49.599 --> 00:05:52.477
All members but Sharnid
are in front of the flag?

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.145
That means...

00:05:54.145 --> 00:05:56.856
Everyone, watch out for a sniping attack!

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:03.154
Dinn!

00:06:03.154 --> 00:06:05.490
Don't worry. Go on ahead!

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.117
Okay!

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:19.295
I mustn't... lose!

00:06:31.766 --> 00:06:36.146
You plan to take me on
with a cheap technique like that?

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:40.984
Let's see if it's cheap or not!

00:07:04.799 --> 00:07:06.634
There!

00:07:08.303 --> 00:07:10.138
Not bad.

00:07:10.472 --> 00:07:12.474
Don't screw with me!

00:07:21.816 --> 00:07:22.984
Why?

00:07:22.984 --> 00:07:24.986
Because you're an idiot.

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:29.157
Knowing yet doing nothing is idiocy, right?

00:07:29.991 --> 00:07:32.827
I came here to end this.

00:07:34.162 --> 00:07:36.873
You asked me "Why?" Siena...

00:07:36.873 --> 00:07:39.834
Well why didn't <i>you </i>stop me?

00:07:40.251 --> 00:07:44.255
What gives you the right to say that?!

00:07:44.255 --> 00:07:46.800
Why do you think this has happened?!

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.261
It's because, Sharnid, you broke your promise!

00:07:50.261 --> 00:07:53.723
And did our promise have that much worth?

00:07:53.723 --> 00:07:59.437
Siena, did you really,
truly take that promise seriously?

00:07:59.437 --> 00:08:01.690
You should've known...

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:04.859
There was no sincerity to our promise!

00:08:04.859 --> 00:08:07.028
All three of us made that oath

00:08:07.028 --> 00:08:09.114
fooling ourselves that what we felt was true.

00:08:09.114 --> 00:08:10.740
Isn't that so, Siena?!

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.575
Shut up!

00:08:16.955 --> 00:08:19.165
Do you mean what you're saying?

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.001
Yeah. I mean it.

00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:24.587
Dinn really is thinking of the city.

00:08:24.587 --> 00:08:29.592
True, it may have started
with his feelings for our leader,

00:08:29.592 --> 00:08:32.220
but he truly cares about this city's--

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.097
Yes, I know!

00:08:34.097 --> 00:08:36.641
Then why do you interfere?

00:08:36.641 --> 00:08:40.437
Because this way is wrong!

00:08:40.437 --> 00:08:43.189
How can you say it's wrong?

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:46.776
Trying to make your
abilities match how you feel...

00:08:46.776 --> 00:08:50.196
How can you just say it's wrong?!

00:08:58.788 --> 00:09:02.792
If what he's doing <i>isn't </i>wrong,

00:09:02.792 --> 00:09:06.796
then why didn't he tell
you about the Overload?

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:10.633
Why didn't he let you use it?

00:09:10.633 --> 00:09:11.760
Shut up.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.014
He felt guilty, so he
didn't tell anyone... not even you.

00:09:16.014 --> 00:09:18.433
That's it, isn't it?!

00:09:20.685 --> 00:09:25.065
I thought I told you to shut up!

00:09:27.484 --> 00:09:28.693
They're coming.

00:09:28.693 --> 00:09:30.695
Shit! Already?

00:09:34.074 --> 00:09:37.744
How come?! I had an
understanding with the local family!

00:09:37.744 --> 00:09:40.080
I guess Gedosh has got something big.

00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:42.791
Please work...

00:09:42.791 --> 00:09:45.085
We're lucky. Saya!

00:09:45.085 --> 00:09:46.127
Yes?

00:09:46.127 --> 00:09:47.462
You stay here and hold down the fort,

00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:49.798
and I'll go and give them what for. Okay?

00:09:49.798 --> 00:09:50.882
Sure.

00:09:50.882 --> 00:09:54.177
This room is already under my protection.

00:09:56.513 --> 00:09:59.974
So, it seems he has no power over machines.

00:09:59.974 --> 00:10:01.810
Be careful.

00:10:10.777 --> 00:10:12.612
Hey there, Leerin.

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:16.574
Where do you think you're going?
A night out on the town just won't do.

00:10:16.574 --> 00:10:18.410
Uh, n-no...

00:10:23.248 --> 00:10:24.874
Wh-What?!

00:10:26.126 --> 00:10:30.130
You're gloomy. Let's go get a drink.

00:10:31.506 --> 00:10:34.092
S-Senior! I'm underage!

00:10:34.092 --> 00:10:36.720
It'll be fine. They have soft drinks, too.

00:10:40.598 --> 00:10:47.480
Even I know that Layfon's
getting expelled couldn't be helped

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:51.735
and that he's really trying his hardest now.

00:10:51.735 --> 00:10:53.153
But still...

00:10:53.153 --> 00:10:57.657
But is it bad for me to think
that one day he can come back,

00:10:57.657 --> 00:11:00.577
that one day it will be all right?

00:11:01.411 --> 00:11:03.413
It's not bad, right?!

00:11:04.247 --> 00:11:06.166
Please listen, Senior!

00:11:06.166 --> 00:11:10.128
I have been listening. For six hours.

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.050
But isn't it cruel?

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:19.054
"You should resign yourself to that fact."

00:11:19.054 --> 00:11:23.266
Sounds like she's already
saying he won't be coming back!

00:11:26.269 --> 00:11:30.982
I won't resign myself to that. Not at all.

00:11:34.778 --> 00:11:36.738
But Leerin...

00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:40.492
No one can stop them.

00:11:59.135 --> 00:12:01.429
<i>Such incredibly strong kei!</i>

00:12:01.429 --> 00:12:04.265
<i>At this rate, it will rupture.</i>

00:12:14.943 --> 00:12:17.153
Who... are you?

00:12:18.113 --> 00:12:19.739
Restoration.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.367
Here I come.

00:12:44.347 --> 00:12:46.766
You shouldn't overdo it.

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:49.978
If you're not careful,
you'll rupture your kei artery.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.106
You don't understand, do you?

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:58.987
You have no idea how
it feels to have a duty forced upon you

00:12:58.987 --> 00:13:05.035
when you know full well
you don't have what it takes yet!

00:13:06.286 --> 00:13:11.458
It's not as if everything
in my life has gone perfectly.

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:14.502
In fact, I'm here because of my failures.

00:13:14.502 --> 00:13:17.088
Being strong won't make things go well.

00:13:17.088 --> 00:13:20.091
People fail when they can't do things well.

00:13:20.091 --> 00:13:25.638
And <i>you </i>couldn't do well.
You made the worst possible choice.

00:13:26.431 --> 00:13:28.767
And who decided that?

00:13:33.938 --> 00:13:35.357
Dinn...

00:13:39.944 --> 00:13:42.155
Don't tell me...

00:13:48.119 --> 00:13:49.954
A Fallen One.

00:13:50.914 --> 00:13:54.000
So everyone's finally here.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.462
They bring misfortune to the strong.

00:13:57.462 --> 00:13:58.630
Misfortune...

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:02.217
It's said they're sensitive to conflict.

00:14:02.217 --> 00:14:06.012
So if there's a competition
and you pick up their presence...

00:14:06.012 --> 00:14:08.515
I'd like you to let yours truly know.

00:14:08.515 --> 00:14:13.853
Otherwise, what happened
at that ruined city will happen here.

00:14:14.646 --> 00:14:16.564
All I must do is let you know?

00:14:16.564 --> 00:14:22.987
Of course. Then we get our
Fallen One and you don't have to worry.

00:14:22.987 --> 00:14:25.198
Everybody's happy.

00:14:26.449 --> 00:14:28.785
Thanks for the info.

00:14:28.785 --> 00:14:30.328
You deceived me!

00:14:30.328 --> 00:14:32.497
Now, that's not nice.

00:14:32.497 --> 00:14:37.127
Yours truly was just selective
about what information I gave you.

00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:40.380
You said they bring
misfortune to the strong...

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:44.300
but you didn't mean
strong military artists, did you?

00:14:45.927 --> 00:14:50.265
What the Fallen Ones want
are those with more spiritual power...

00:14:50.265 --> 00:14:54.185
Those with strong wills and hearts.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:59.649
Excellently observed.
That's the president's sister for you.

00:15:00.442 --> 00:15:04.362
Well, I'll just be takin' it, as promised.

00:15:05.613 --> 00:15:07.240
Fon-Fon...

00:15:11.578 --> 00:15:14.205
What are you doing?

00:15:23.465 --> 00:15:26.343
<i>It's controlling Dinn?</i>

00:15:26.343 --> 00:15:28.678
<i>Then I'll...</i>

00:15:29.262 --> 00:15:31.890
It's our prey.

00:15:38.021 --> 00:15:43.193
If you can just suppress the host,
it's easy to capture a Fallen One.

00:15:43.193 --> 00:15:47.322
It sure was a stroke of luck
that it came to the academic city.

00:15:47.322 --> 00:15:52.160
He may have lofty ideals,
but he hasn't got the skills to back that up.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:54.954
He can't make full
use of the Fallen One's gifts.

00:15:54.954 --> 00:15:57.624
This is all too easy.

00:15:57.624 --> 00:16:00.794
What will you do with him
when you take him to Glendan?

00:16:00.794 --> 00:16:05.256
You can't even go back to Glendan,
so that doesn't concern you.

00:16:05.256 --> 00:16:06.591
Wait!

00:16:06.591 --> 00:16:08.468
I can't let you take Dinn Dee!

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.554
I'm not listening.

00:16:11.554 --> 00:16:14.224
To be sure, what he did was wrong...

00:16:14.224 --> 00:16:18.645
But we are also comrades of the same school.

00:16:18.645 --> 00:16:23.733
I won't entrust his fate
to you maggots. I won't have it!

00:16:23.733 --> 00:16:25.068
Release Dinn Dee!

00:16:25.068 --> 00:16:30.740
And what do you plan to do if I don't?
Fight? Against yours truly?

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:35.578
You're going to make the Salinban
Mercenary Training Group an enemy?

00:16:36.413 --> 00:16:38.248
Don't go getting cocky.

00:16:38.248 --> 00:16:42.335
Did you say something? <i>Former </i>Heaven's Blade?

00:16:42.335 --> 00:16:45.046
I will be your opponent.

00:16:45.046 --> 00:16:50.552
You'll be just right for shaking
the rust off my Saiharden techniques.

00:16:50.552 --> 00:16:52.178
Restoration.

00:16:54.639 --> 00:16:57.308
Even now, you're using a dual-edged sword?

00:16:57.308 --> 00:17:00.353
You're good at makin' fun of people.

00:17:00.353 --> 00:17:04.649
Fine! If I mop you up and go back to Glendan,

00:17:04.649 --> 00:17:09.404
I might even be able to get
the Heaven's Blade you left behind.

00:17:09.404 --> 00:17:10.405
Layfon!

00:17:10.405 --> 00:17:12.407
I will get Dinn back.

00:17:16.161 --> 00:17:17.328
Felli.

00:17:17.328 --> 00:17:18.747
Yes?

00:17:18.747 --> 00:17:22.876
Are you in contact with the student
council president? Connect me.

00:17:22.876 --> 00:17:23.710
It is I.

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:26.046
Did you anticipate things coming to this?

00:17:26.046 --> 00:17:30.592
I hadn't heard how the
Fallen One would be captured.

00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:36.097
But of course, we cannot
simply let him take Dinn with him.

00:17:36.097 --> 00:17:37.891
Then what do we do?!

00:17:37.891 --> 00:17:42.771
Is there not some way
to separate it from Dinn?

00:17:42.771 --> 00:17:47.275
Why did it choose Dinn?
Unless we know that...

00:17:47.275 --> 00:17:48.360
I know.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:49.194
What?!

00:17:49.194 --> 00:17:51.154
The Fallen Ones may
select who they possess

00:17:51.154 --> 00:17:53.823
based on strength of sentiment.

00:17:53.823 --> 00:17:57.410
Because they are out-of-control
city spirits, that sentiment may be

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:02.582
the desire to protect a city.
Or something similar.

00:18:02.582 --> 00:18:06.211
Because it feels the same as Dinn...

00:18:06.211 --> 00:18:08.838
But any of us feel that.

00:18:09.339 --> 00:18:13.385
Perhaps it's because that sentiment
was in its ultimate state.

00:18:13.385 --> 00:18:16.471
The moment he was defeated by Layfon...

00:18:16.471 --> 00:18:21.393
His sense of responsibility, that he must
protect the city, was made clear.

00:18:21.393 --> 00:18:25.021
It was the moment his
sentiment was at its peak.

00:18:25.021 --> 00:18:28.525
Perhaps, too, it was that these two resonated...

00:18:28.525 --> 00:18:31.194
both bitter at the loss
of their sense of purpose.

00:18:31.194 --> 00:18:35.824
Then at this rate,
won't separating them be impossible?

00:18:36.241 --> 00:18:40.745
Our only choice is to break his spirit again.

00:18:41.162 --> 00:18:44.374
Why don't ya leave that to me?

00:18:46.376 --> 00:18:47.669
Y-You two!

00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:49.921
But... Can you?

00:18:50.755 --> 00:18:53.383
Don't got much choice, do we?

00:18:58.555 --> 00:19:04.477
Why don't you use a proper blade?
That's your specialty, right?

00:19:04.477 --> 00:19:05.729
It's a tradeoff.

00:19:05.729 --> 00:19:12.193
You're an idiot. A moron who
mocks battle by not using what he can use!

00:19:12.193 --> 00:19:16.489
I've chosen not to use them.
It's my conviction...

00:19:17.615 --> 00:19:23.455
Someone who fights for no one's
benefit couldn't possibly understand.

00:19:23.455 --> 00:19:25.457
You've gone too far.

00:19:34.674 --> 00:19:36.885
Dammit! Where'd he go?

00:19:40.764 --> 00:19:42.182
Restoration!

00:19:44.601 --> 00:19:46.019
Siena!

00:20:03.703 --> 00:20:05.914
Dammit!

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.595
C'mon, make it!

00:20:22.305 --> 00:20:23.306
Siena!

00:20:23.306 --> 00:20:25.058
Leave it to me!

00:20:27.852 --> 00:20:29.187
Up ahead. Hurry!

00:20:29.187 --> 00:20:30.814
Thank you.

00:20:34.859 --> 00:20:38.279
Ah. I see. I'm already...

00:20:57.173 --> 00:20:58.591
Dinn.

00:21:01.678 --> 00:21:03.096
Dinn.

00:21:05.056 --> 00:21:08.852
Dinn... We're finished.

00:21:08.852 --> 00:21:13.356
There's no more need to fight.

00:21:14.441 --> 00:21:18.570
There are people who
think the same way we do.

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:23.491
We can leave it to them,
and our promise still won't be broken.

00:21:23.491 --> 00:21:24.909
So...

00:21:25.785 --> 00:21:27.203
So...

00:21:31.249 --> 00:21:35.170
You've worked hard enough. It's okay now.

00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:37.422
Dinn...

00:21:52.937 --> 00:21:54.773
I loved you.

00:22:06.326 --> 00:22:09.079
I loved you. And...

00:22:19.297 --> 00:22:22.967
And... this is goodbye.

00:22:26.262 --> 00:22:36.356
<i>Haikei, anata wa dare o omotteimasu ka</i>

00:22:36.356 --> 00:22:43.446
<i>Kono tegami wa mada mune no naka</i>

00:22:43.446 --> 00:22:53.498
<i>Totsuzen fureta anata no kioku no kakera</i>

00:22:53.498 --> 00:23:00.588
<i>Kokoro ni sasatte, ugokenai</i>

00:23:00.588 --> 00:23:05.468
<i>Kizuite hoshii, kizukanaide</i>

00:23:05.468 --> 00:23:09.139
<i>Tsumetaku suru no wa koi no sei? </i>

00:23:09.139 --> 00:23:18.732
<i>Tsutaetai yo, soba ni ite yo, demo ienai</i>

00:23:19.524 --> 00:23:28.116
<i>Yogoreta kono sekai de anata ni deaeta yo</i>

00:23:28.116 --> 00:23:39.294
<i>Watashi no kokoro ni maiorita</i>
<i>kiseki kanadete kudasai</i>

00:23:39.294 --> 00:23:47.302
<i>Ai no Zuellni</i>

00:23:54.184 --> 00:23:55.810
<i>In preparation for their next competition,</i>

